{1}{[The wrapped figure draws back from your light.] Another blade? Wait. Please. I have not harmed your farmers. If you have come to kill me, at least hear what that would mean.}{[The wrapped figure draws back from your light.] Another blade? Wait. Please. I have not harmed your farmers. If you have come to kill me, at least hear what that would mean.}{}{}{}{}
{2}{Tell me who you are.}{}{1}{}{20}{}
{3}{The town says you are dangerous.}{}{1}{}{40}{}
{4}{Let us discuss what happens next.}{}{1}{}{60}{}
{5}{I came for the bounty. Defend yourself.}{}{1}{}{-35}{}
{6}{Goodbye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{20}{Amtut. Once a king, though the kingdom is dust now. I ruled fairly until I began to fear dying. Then I sent men across the world to save me. Some returned empty-handed. I had them executed.}{Amtut. Once a king, though the kingdom is dust now. I ruled fairly until I began to fear dying. Then I sent men across the world to save me. Some returned empty-handed. I had them executed.}{}{}{}{}
{21}{You murdered them for failing you.}{}{1}{}{30}{}
{22}{How did you become like this?}{}{1}{}{50}{}
{23}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{30}{Yes. Not an illness. Not an adviser whispering in my ear. My order. I sent men to their deaths because I feared my own. I have had rather a long time to consider that.}{Yes. Not an illness. Not an adviser whispering in my ear. My order. I sent men to their deaths because I feared my own. I have had rather a long time to consider that.}{}{}{}{}
{31}{Regret does not undo it.}{}{1}{}{35}{}
{32}{But it may change what you do now.}{}{1}{}{35}{}
{33}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{35}{Nothing undoes it. I cannot ask their forgiveness, and yours is not theirs to give. I can only stop adding to the harm.}{Nothing undoes it. I cannot ask their forgiveness, and yours is not theirs to give. I can only stop adding to the harm.}{}{}{}{}
{36}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{40}{I walked out beneath the moon. A farmer leapt from hiding with an axe. I ran. The sheep screamed, he shouted, and by morning I was an army of the dead. I should never have gone near his home.}{I walked out beneath the moon. A farmer leapt from hiding with an axe. I ran. The sheep screamed, he shouted, and by morning I was an army of the dead. I should never have gone near his home.}{}{}{}{}
{41}{He admits that he swung first.}{}{1}{qu 1404 4}{45}{}
{42}{Fear alone does not make you harmless.}{}{1}{}{45}{}
{43}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{45}{No. I was capable of cruelty long before these wrappings. Judge what I do, not merely how wretched I look. But let the farmer sleep without another midnight visitor.}{No. I was capable of cruelty long before these wrappings. Judge what I do, not merely how wretched I look. But let the farmer sleep without another midnight visitor.}{}{}{}{}
{46}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{50}{A stranger promised life after death for every heartstone in my kingdom. Only afterward did he explain the rest: destroy this body without a heartstone, and my soul stays imprisoned in it. A killer carrying one can release me. He had taken them all.}{A stranger promised life after death for every heartstone in my kingdom. Only afterward did he explain the rest: destroy this body without a heartstone, and my soul stays imprisoned in it. A killer carrying one can release me. He had taken them all.}{}{}{}{}
{51}{There is a book about you in the library.}{}{1}{}{55}{}
{52}{Heartstones still exist. Your kingdom was not the whole world.}{}{1}{}{55}{}
{53}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{55}{Then perhaps the world has kept one kindness for me. Ask the librarian. I cannot face another axe without knowing whether it brings an end or a smaller prison.}{Then perhaps the world has kept one kindness for me. Ask the librarian. I cannot face another axe without knowing whether it brings an end or a smaller prison.}{}{}{}{gv 830 1, qu 1408 2}
{56}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{60}{I want the fear to end. Some days I want everything to end. But I will not choose for you, and I will not have you choose blindly for me.}{I want the fear to end. Some days I want everything to end. But I will not choose for you, and I will not have you choose blindly for me.}{}{}{}{}
{61}{Tell me about the curse first.}{}{1}{gv 830 0}{50}{}
{62}{We can release your soul with a heartstone.}{}{1}{gv 830 1}{70}{}
{63}{Would you live here peacefully if the town left you alone?}{}{1}{}{100}{}
{64}{I will kill you without a heartstone.}{}{1}{gv 830 1}{80}{}
{65}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{70}{[He steadies his hands.] Yes. With the stone here, I can accept it. Do not call it redemption. Let it simply be an end.}{[He steadies his hands.] Yes. With the stone here, I can accept it. Do not call it redemption. Let it simply be an end.}{}{}{}{}
{71}{You have my compassion, not absolution. I will help you.}{}{1}{in 5683}{-9}{}
{72}{I will release you, but I will not forgive those murders.}{}{1}{in 5683}{-9}{}
{73}{I need to fetch a heartstone first.}{}{1}{ni 5683}{90}{}
{74}{Not yet.}{}{1}{}{60}{}
{80}{Then the town will have its peace, and I shall have only these bones. I have deserved punishment. I do not know that anyone deserves forever.}{Then the town will have its peace, and I shall have only these bones. I have deserved punishment. I do not know that anyone deserves forever.}{}{}{}{}
{81}{I understand. Draw your last breath.}{}{1}{}{-35}{}
{82}{No. There is another way.}{}{1}{}{60}{}
{90}{Bring a heartstone in your own pack when you return. A promise of one is not enough. The librarian may know where to find it.}{Bring a heartstone in your own pack when you return. A promise of one is not enough. The librarian may know where to find it.}{}{}{}{}
{91}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{100}{This chamber would be enough. No farms, no roads, no visitors frightened in the dark. I swear it. But will they keep their hunters out? Get the farmer and the mayor to agree before you promise me safety.}{This chamber would be enough. No farms, no roads, no visitors frightened in the dark. I swear it. But will they keep their hunters out? Get the farmer and the mayor to agree before you promise me safety.}{}{}{}{gv 822 1, qu 1409 2}
{101}{I will speak to both of them.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{102}{Both have agreed. This chamber is your refuge.}{}{1}{gv 823 1, gv 824 1}{-21}{}
{103}{I have another question.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{150}{An agreement with only one side is merely a hope. Speak to Pollock and Mayor Gray, then return to me.}{An agreement with only one side is merely a hope. Speak to Pollock and Mayor Gray, then return to me.}{}{}{}{}
{151}{Goodbye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{300}{The silence is different now. Not safe forever, perhaps, but not another hunt. I will keep my word. Go and live a life that does not need centuries of excuses.}{The silence is different now. Not safe forever, perhaps, but not another hunt. I will keep my word. Go and live a life that does not need centuries of excuses.}{}{}{}{}
{301}{Goodbye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{400}{There is nothing more to bargain over. What was done cannot be paid away.}{There is nothing more to bargain over. What was done cannot be paid away.}{}{}{}{}
{401}{Goodbye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
